HST Office: feature search (Alt+Q, "Tìm tính năng…") ranks results, names their place on the ribbon and
fills the empty box.

- sfx2/source/commandpopup/CommandPopup.cxx, sfx2/inc/commandpopup/CommandPopup.hxx:
  - Ranking: one score per entry instead of five passes (scoreMatch). The own label (menu or ribbon
    button) counts most: the whole label, then the label starting with the text up to a word end, a
    whole word, the label starting with it, a word starting with it; then the search keywords of
    FeatureSearch.xcu (whole word before word start), then the menu/ribbon path, then every typed
    word anywhere (the old last pass). A match inside a word ranks below every word-start match.
    HST commands (+8) and commands with keywords, the often used ones (+5), move up within a rank,
    so "tien" lists "Định dạng tiền VND" before "Ngôn ngữ giao diện ▸ Tiếng Việt". Equal ranks keep
    the menu order. tests/unit/test_feature_search_ux.py mirrors the scoring.
  - Ribbon location: when the window shows the ribbon (Tabbed notebookbar), the tabs are read when
    the search opens (tab text and the command and text of every toolbox button, also inside groups
    folded into a "Group ▾" button; regular tabs before contextual ones). A result on the ribbon
    reads "Tab ▸ Button" ("Xem lại ▸ Đếm từ"); other results keep the menu path. Commands only on
    the ribbon are indexed too. Nothing is hard-coded, so a reworked ribbon is picked up as is.
  - Commands that have search keywords but are in no menu and on no ribbon tab (items of a popup
    menu built at run time, e.g. Sheets "Định dạng có điều kiện ▸ Giá trị trùng lặp",
    .uno:ConditionalFormatEasy?FormatRule:short=8) are indexed under their own label when the module
    has a label for the command, so another application's commands stay out.
  - Commands without an SFX slot (Slides ".uno:InsertSlide", "Trang chiếu mới") are offered when
    the frame has a dispatcher for them, as add-on commands already were; they were dropped, so
    "trang chieu moi" found nothing.
  - Empty box: the 5 commands last run from the search in this module, then 5 suggestions of the
    module (/org.hasontech.hstoffice.FeatureSearch: Recent, Suggestions; search.xcs and
    FeatureSearch.xcu of the bundled HST extension). Nothing is selected, so Enter in the empty box
    runs nothing. Without the extension the box stays empty as before.

